// TEST: a scalar base to a generic exponent the call makes an array (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019 @ 7:12
// ERROR-CONTAINS: makes that exponent an ARRAY
// `2.0 ^ n` is typed as its base -- the exponent of `^` never decides the
// power's type (docs/formalism.md section 2.4) -- so an array exponent has no
// shape to land in: refused at the call (it reached g++ as BL9002).
function tw(n) = 2.0 ^ n
let r = tw([1, 2])
